<title>SWITZERLAND: Jan-Feb 97 world air cargo up 7.8pct -ACI.</title>
<headline>Jan-Feb 97 world air cargo up 7.8pct -ACI.</headline>
<dateline>GENEVA 1997-06-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Freight and mail traffic handled by 486 airports around the world in January-February 1997 totalled 7,870,515 tonnes, up 7.8 percent on the same period in 1996, according to provisional figures issued by Airports Council International (ACI).</p>
<p>Cargo traffic handled by airports in Geneva-based ACI's six geographical regions in January-February 1997, with percentage change on January-February 1996, was as follows:</p>
<p>		     Jan-Feb 1997  Pct change from Jan-Feb 96</p>
<p>  Africa		33,437 tonnes     up  1.3</p>
<p>  Asia/Pacific   1,650,875		up 11.4</p>
<p>  Europe	   1,595,214		up  3.6</p>
<p>  LatAm/Carib	189,853		up  3.3</p>
<p>  Middle East	238,748		up  6.5</p>
<p>  North America  4,162,388		up  8.4</p>
<p>  Total	    7,870,515		up  7.8</p>
<p>- Reuters Air Cargo Service Tel+ 44 171 542 7706 Fax +5017 - www.racs.com</p>
